# Machine facts for the Balam deploy scripts (ADR-0013).
#
# Copy to deploy/deploy.env (git-ignored) ONLY if the derived defaults are wrong
# for this machine. Every value below is optional: deploy/lib.sh works them out
# from the machine itself — the user running the installer, that user's home, the
# checkout the script lives in, and the tools actually on PATH. A deployment on a
# plain `ubuntu`-style host needs no deploy.env at all.
#
# These values are substituted into the *.service.in templates when the install
# scripts render them into /etc/systemd/system. Changing one means re-running the
# installer; editing the unit in /etc/ is pointless, it gets overwritten.
#
# Secrets never live here — they belong in the repo .env. This file holds paths.

# The OS user every unit runs as.            default: whoever runs the installer
#BALAM_USER=ubuntu

# That user's home. Only needed when it is not what getent reports.
#BALAM_HOME=/home/ubuntu

# Where extra instances (install-instance.sh) are checked out, and the basename
# they are prefixed with: <root>/<prefix>-<name>.
# defaults: the parent directory and the basename of THIS checkout, so an
# instance lands next to the primary — /srv/balam -> /srv/balam-work.
#BALAM_INSTANCE_ROOT=/home/ubuntu/projects
#BALAM_INSTANCE_PREFIX=balam

# Absolute paths to the binaries the units exec. Defaults come from `command -v`
# with a conventional fallback, because systemd resolves ExecStart before PATH
# applies and a bare name would not be found.
#BALAM_UV=/home/ubuntu/.local/bin/uv
#BALAM_BUN=/home/ubuntu/.bun/bin/bun
#BALAM_CLOUDFLARED=/usr/local/bin/cloudflared
#BALAM_OPENCODE=/home/ubuntu/.opencode/bin/opencode

# OpenCode's SQLite database (AGENT_BACKEND=opencode only).
#BALAM_OPENCODE_DB=/home/ubuntu/.local/share/opencode/balam.db

# PATH for the units, and so for every shell the agent's Bash tool spawns —
# systemd sources no profile, so anything missing here is missing for the agent.
# The default is probed from the toolchains actually installed under BALAM_HOME
# (bun, .local/bin, the highest nvm node, cargo, go) plus the system defaults.
# Set it only to pin an exact list.
#BALAM_UNIT_PATH=/home/ubuntu/.bun/bin:/home/ubuntu/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
#BALAM_GOPATH=/home/ubuntu/go

# Which Claude account the FIRST instance's bot runs as (claude_sdk backend).
# Unset — the default — leaves it on ~/.claude, which is right when the machine
# runs one bot and nobody uses `claude` interactively on it.
#
# Set it when ~/.claude is a PERSON's login rather than the bot's. Otherwise the
# bot's account is whatever that person last ran `claude auth login` as, and the
# two share one rate limit. Extra instances are always pinned, by balam@.service.
#BALAM_PRIMARY_CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/ubuntu/.claude-bot

# Where install-instance.sh seeds a new Claude config dir from (skills symlink,
# settings.json, CLAUDE.md). A fresh config dir has none of these, and the SDK
# backend asks for setting_sources=["user", ...] with skills="all" — so without
# seeding the new bot sees no global skills and sends every tool call to the
# approval keyboard. Defaults to the operator's ~/.claude.
#BALAM_SEED_FROM=/home/ubuntu/.claude

# The named tunnel for the first instance: `cloudflared tunnel run <name>`, with
# ingress installed at /etc/cloudflared/<name>.yml.
#BALAM_TUNNEL_NAME=balam
